    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0708" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.61333/824: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-22T11:15:00-03:00">June 22, 1943—11:15
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 28—4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–1310. Reference my airgram A–1174, June 11, 10 a.m.…</p>
                <p>Sr. Valentim Bouças<anchor n="88" xml:id="d640-f1"/> informed the Embassy
                    yesterday that President Vargas has strongly disapproved of Guedes’<anchor
                        n="89" xml:id="d640-f2"/> action in increasing <pb facs="0709" n="697"
                        xml:id="pg697"/> coffee prices following the entry into the market of the
                    United States Quartermaster. Bouças said: “I would not be surprised if President
                    Vargas made a gift of a substantial quantity of coffee to the Armed Forces of
                    the United States Government”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d640-f1" n="88" xml:id="d640-f1-content">
                <p>Executive Secretary, Commission for the Control of the Washington Agreements.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d640-f2" n="89" xml:id="d640-f2-content">
                <p>Jayme Fernandes Guedes, President, National Coffee Department.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
